        "consistency_ledger": "# BINDING CONSISTENCY LEDGER — Northern Welsh (Gogledd Cymru Welsh) Listening Pod\n\n## 1. TRANSLITERATION\nTRANSLITERATION: not needed — names stay as written.\n\n## 2. PRICES\n£2.80 (coffee) → dwy bunt wyth deg ceiniog\n£3.50 (coffee+cake) → tri phunt hanner\n£4.50 (pint) → pedwar punt hanner\n£8.40 (multiple coffees) → wyth punt pedwar deg ceiniog\n£12.50 (taxi) → deuddeg punt hanner\n\n## 3. TARGET-LANGUAGE NAME\nCymraeg (when learners refer to \"Northern Welsh (colloquial Gogledd Cymru Welsh)\", render as \"Cymraeg\" in natural Northern speech)\n\n## 4. RECURRING LINES\n- \"Good morning\" / \"Good afternoon\" / \"Good evening\" → \"Bore da\" / \"Prynhawn da\" / \"Nos da\"\n- \"What can I get you?\" → \"Be ga i i ti?\" (ti register, peer) or \"Be ga i chi?\" (chi register, staff to customer)\n- \"Please\" (softened, not bare \"plis\") → omit or use \"os gweli di'n dda\" (ti) / \"os gwelwch yn dda\" (chi, formal); tone carries politeness\n- \"Thank you\" / \"Thank you very much\" → \"Diolch\" / \"Diolch yn fawr iawn\"\n- \"You're welcome\" → \"Croeso\" or \"Popeth yn iawn\"\n- \"Goodbye\" / \"See you\" / \"See you later\" → \"Hwyl\" / \"Hwyl fawr\" / \"Wela i di\"\n- \"Excuse me\" → \"Esgusodwch fi\" (chi, formal) / \"Sciwsiwch fi\" (colloquial)\n- \"Could I / Can I have…?\" → \"Ga i…?\" (ti) / \"Gawn ni…?\" (ni, group) / \"Oes posib i mi gael…?\" (more formal)\n- \"How far is it…?\" → \"Faint ydy hi i…?\"\n- \"Is this seat taken?\" → \"Ydy'r sedd yma'n rhydd?\"\n- \"Do you have…?\" → \"Oes gen ti…?\" (ti) / \"Oes gennych chi…?\" (chi)\n- \"Could I pay by card / Do you have contactless?\" → \"Ga i dalu efo cerdyn?\" / \"Oes contactless gennych chi?\"\n- \"That's [price] altogether\" → \"Dyna [price] i gyd\" or \"Pump punt dau ddeg, plis\"\n- \"I'm sorry / I'm sorry but…\" → \"Sori\" or \"Sori ond…\" (Northern colloquial, not formal apologetic)\n- \"I'm learning Cymraeg\" → \"Dw i'n dysgu Cymraeg\"\n- \"Could you say that again?\" / \"Say that again?\" → \"Fedri di ddweud hynna eto?\" (ti) / \"Allwch chi ddweud hynna eto?\" (chi)\n- \"Where is the [item]?\" → \"Lle ma'r [item]?\" or \"Lle mae'r [item]?\"\n- \"It's on your left / right\" → \"Ma' fo ar dy chwith / dde di\" or \"Ma' fo ar eich chwith / dde chi\"\n- \"How much is that?\" → \"Faint ydy hwnna?\" or \"Be' ydy'r pris?\"\n- \"Can we pay?\" → \"Gawn ni dalu?\"\n- \"Thank you for your help / kindness\" → \"Diolch am dy help / ti'n garedig\" (ti) / \"Diolch am eich help / chi'n garedig\" (chi)\n\n## 5. REGISTER\n- **Customer–staff (unfamiliar, neutral age):** Chi (formal plural/respectful) — staff use chi to customers; customers reciprocate chi to staff they don't know.\n- **Strangers (peer, young-to-middle-aged):** Ti (informal) — natural among locals/acquaintances of similar age in casual venues.\n- **Friends:** Ti (informal) — consistent throughout.\n- **Older/respected staff or customers:** Chi (formal) — reciprocal respect.\n\n## 6. SPEAKER GENDER\nSPEAKER GENDER: not marked in Northern Welsh (colloquial Gogledd Cymru Welsh) — skip."
      },
