        "consistency_ledger": "# BINDING CONSISTENCY LEDGER — Northern Welsh (Colloquial Gogledd Cymru Welsh) Listening Pod\n\n## 1. TRANSLITERATION\nTRANSLITERATION: not needed — names stay as written.\n\n## 2. PRICES\n- £3 → tair punt\n- £5.50 → pump punt a hanner\n- £6–£8 (coffee + cake) → rhyw saith punt\n- £4.50–£6 (pint) → rhyw bum punt\n- £8.40 (Scene 7 total) → wyth punt dau ddeg\n- £12.50 (Scene 14 taxi) → deuddeg punt hanner\n\n## 3. TARGET-LANGUAGE NAME\n**Cymraeg** — used identically in all scenes where the language is named aloud.\n\n## 4. RECURRING LINES\n\n| Canonical | Northern Welsh (Colloquial) |\n|-----------|---------------------------|\n| Good morning. | Bore da. |\n| Good afternoon. | Prynhawn da. |\n| Good evening. | Noswaith dda. |\n| What can I get you? | Be alla i 'i gael i chdi? |\n| Thank you very much. Goodbye. | Diolch yn fawr. Hwyl. |\n| Excuse me. | Scusio fi. |\n| Pleased to meet you. | Tŷ lân 'i chi gwrdd â chdi. |\n| Where are you from? | O ble dach chi'n dwad? |\n| I'm learning Northern Welsh. | Dw i'n dysgu Cymraeg. |\n| Could you say that again more slowly? | Fedri di ddeud hynna eto'n arafach? |\n| I'd like a [drink], please. | Liciwn i [drink], os gweli di'n dda. |\n| Would you like to sit-in or takeaway? | Yma isio di'r gwmnniaeth neu mynd â fo? |\n| Could I pay by card? Do you have contactless? | Fedra i dalu â cherdyn? Oes gynnoch chi dap? |\n| Are you here on holiday? | Wyt ti yma ar wyliau? |\n| You speak very good Northern Welsh. | Dach chi'n siarad Cymraeg yn dda iawn. |\n| Thank you very much, and goodbye. | Diolch yn fawr, a hwyl. |\n| Excuse me, do you know how to get to [place]? | Scusio fi, wyt ti'n gwybod sut i fynd i [place]? |\n| Thank you very much. You've been very helpful. | Diolch yn fawr. Ti 'di bod yn dda iawn. |\n| Can you take me to [place], please? | Fedri di fy nymryd i i [place], os gweli di'n dda? |\n| Could I pay by card? | Fedra i dalu â cherdyn? |\n| I'm learning Northern Welsh. I need to practise more to speak Northern Welsh better. | Dw i'n dysgu Cymraeg. Dw i angen ymarfer mwy i siarad Cymraeg yn well. |\n| You seem to speak it very well. I can understand you easily. | Dach chi'n siarad yn dda iawn. Dw i'n dallt chi'n iawn. |\n| I don't understand people very well when they don't speak slowly. | Dw i ddim yn dallt pobol yn dda iawn pan dydyn nhw ddim yn siarad yn araf. |\n\n## 5. REGISTER\n\n**Unmarked polite register throughout:** Use **ti** universally for all service workers (barista, bartender, shop assistant, pharmacist, taxi driver, hotel receptionist), strangers, acquaintances, and peers. Politeness is carried through softening particles (\"os gweli di'n dda\", \"diolch yn fawr\") rather than pronoun formality. No character uses \"chi\" except where the scene explicitly marks formal institutional context (none in this pod). \n\n**Softening particles:** Questions often drop auxiliary verbs and use rising tone; polite requests use \"os gweli di'n dda\" (if you please) naturally one or twice per scene, not excessively. One or two \"diolch\" per speaker per scene is natural; do not cluster multiple thanks.",
